{"text":"Sunlight reaches Earth's atmosphere and scatters in all directions, but shorter blue wavelengths are scattered more strongly than longer red wavelengths due to a phenomenon known as Rayleigh scattering. This scattered blue light is redirected toward our eyes from all parts of the sky, making the entire dome appear blue rather than just the area directly around the sun. Consequently, we perceive the sky as blue because our eyes are most sensitive to this scattered short-wavelength light.","output_ids":[29108,4009,23716,8964,579,16078,321,1100,9872,303,660,17425,11,694,22602,6105,89661,513,35742,777,16025,1056,4860,2438,89661,4016,310,264,24057,3750,430,12870,60845,69377,13,1061,35742,6105,3000,369,47289,8574,1004,6213,494,660,5306,314,279,12515,11,3154,279,4307,55419,4833,6105,4598,1056,1066,279,2982,5774,2094,279,6797,13,50275,11,567,42918,279,12515,430,6105,1521,1004,6213,513,1379,15739,310,411,35742,2716,2543,33705,3000,13,248046],"meta_info":{"id":"59ca17a58e814743bcdeebdf4e4116b0","finish_reason":{"type":"stop","matched":248046},"prompt_tokens":23,"weight_version":"default","num_retractions":0,"input_token_logprobs":[],"output_token_logprobs":[[-0.1832960546016693,29108,null],[-4.017272294731811e-05,4009,null],[-0.9026355147361755,23716,null],[-0.007720157038420439,8964,null],[-0.28569987416267395,579,null],[-0.0004538459761533886,16078,null],[-0.5541914701461792,321,null],[-0.4649049639701843,1100,null],[-0.0003805628512054682,9872,null],[-0.059259600937366486,303,null],[-0.1150243878364563,660,null],[-0.0004368066438473761,17425,null],[-0.5497450828552246,11,null],[-0.6541821360588074,694,null],[-0.541878342628479,22602,null],[-0.3338099718093872,6105,null],[-0.0599963441491127,89661,null],[-0.43167632818222046,513,null],[-0.04776541516184807,35742,null],[-0.511909544467926,777,null],[-0.1794268786907196,16025,null],[-0.40428781509399414,1056,null],[-0.5008060932159424,4860,null],[-0.0060477592051029205,2438,null],[-0.10995737463235855,89661,null],[-0